+# Incident brief: August–September 2026
+
+Follow-up status as of the 30 September sync.
+
+## 11 August: data backlog and full disk
+
+- **Impact:** Incoming data stalled about 2.5 hours overnight; customers saw stale dashboards, no data lost. The database briefly refused writes at 97% disk.
+- **Cause:** One malformed batch jammed processing, which retried it endlessly; retry logs filled the disk.
+- **Fix:** Restarted processing with the bad batch set aside; cleaned up the database and logs (disk to 61%).
+- **Follow-ups:**
+  - 80% disk alert (Sunil): done.
+  - Stop bad batches jamming processing (Jonas): open, in review.
+  - Paging escalation review (Elif, Sunil): done; unanswered pages escalate after 15 minutes.
+
+## 21 September: expired API certificate
+
+- **Impact:** Public API down 47 minutes Monday morning; nearly all customers and browsers could not connect.
+- **Cause:** The certificate expired; its automatic renewal had failed silently all month after a credential change.
+- **Fix:** Renewed the certificate and restarted the API; renewal failures now alert.
+- **Follow-ups:**
+  - Reminder 14 days before expiry (Priya): done.
+  - Days-left alert (Priya): open.
+  - Expiry check in weekly checklist (Tomasz): open.
+  - Responders record actions as they go (Mara): done, in on-call handover notes.
